a crew-support overhead; reducing rotation frequency (via longer
crew tours) reduces cost but may leave the assembly site
uncrewed during transit windows.

\subsection{Proximity Risk and Operational Safety}

The cumulative proximity risk of
{{ "%.4f"|format(run.result.cumulative_risk) }} was accumulated
over {{ run.result.total_periods }}~periods according to
Eq.~(\ref{eq:risk}).
{% if run.result.cumulative_risk > 0.01 %}
This is a non-trivial risk level, driven primarily by periods in
which crew vehicles were docked simultaneously with cargo
vehicles actively unloading---the $\binom{n}{2}$ pair term grows
quadratically with $n$, so even brief multi-vehicle overlap
intervals contribute disproportionately.
Operational mitigations would include staggered arrival windows
(scheduling cargo arrivals to end before crew docking begins)
and enhanced proximity operations protocols during high-$n$
