\subsection{Launch Count versus Duration Trade-Off}

The Pareto scatter in Fig.~\ref{fig:pareto} shows that reducing
the total number of launches by consolidating payload onto
fewer, larger vehicles tends to lengthen the campaign:
heavy-lift payloads arrive less frequently, so the assembly
crew waits longer between material deliveries, crew-rotation
gaps widen, and partial-assembly (WIP) modules accumulate
without the cargo needed to complete them.
Conversely, schedule-minimal solutions saturate the
pad-turnaround constraint and push launch count toward its
upper bound.
